WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:58.560
[grunting]

3
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.610
<b>Heaven's Gate</b>

4
00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.570
[BLACKBEARD laughing]

5
00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.570
Oh, well. They got away!

6
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.280
[DOC Q coughs]

7
00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.910
What they got is lucky.

8
00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.580
So what? We're just gonna sit
here and let 'em escape?

9
00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.920
We just lost 160-
million-berry bounty

10
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.130
and you're laughin' about it?

11
00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.460
Come on! We gotta do somethin'!

12
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.780
[BLACKBEARD laughs]

13
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.450
Easy, Burgess. They
haven't left this world.

14
00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.080
They'll be back. We'll
meet them soon enough,

15
00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.580
as long as we stay
on the Grand Line.

16
00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.290
This is true. We are but
cogs in the gears of fate.

17
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.180
And though they've managed
to escape us today,

18
00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.210
they cannot outrun destiny.

19
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.090
[BLACKBEARD laughs]

20
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.290
[BLACKBEARD]
Ya see, Burgess?

21
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.660
[BURGESS]
Bah! Whatever.

22
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.580
[DOC Q coughing]

23
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.800
[BLACKBEARD laughing]

24
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.310
What the...?

25
00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.520
What just happened to us?
Everyone all right?

26
00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.820
Hey! Look, guys!
Out there! What is that?

27
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:22.940
[SANJI]
What in the world?

28
00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.850
[LUFFY]
It's solid white!

29
00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:25.890
They're clouds!

30
00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.560
But how? Why aren't we falling?

31
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.680
[LUFFY]
Clouds float.
Boats float. Same thing!

32
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.460
[CHOPPER, SANJI, ZORO]
– No, it's not!
– No, it's not!

33
00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.960
Oh, no! Usopp's not breathing!

34
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.040
He's not?

35
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.540
Someone do something!
Mouth-to-mouth!

36
00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.380
[SANJI]
Right!

37
00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.050
I'll do mouth-to-mouth on Nami!

38
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.260
Moron.

39
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.310
[CHOPPER]
Usopp! Come on, speak to me!

40
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.630
[BOTH]
– He's alive!
– He's alive!

41
00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.220
I am?

42
00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.330
[USOPP]
Then where are we?!

43
00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.270
What's with all these clouds?!

44
00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.520
They're everywhere!

45
00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.960
Basically, it's...
it's an ocean in the sky.

46
00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.510
No way. Seriously?

47
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.440
[NAMI]
But look, the Log
Pose is still pointing up.

48
00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.050
So we must still be
somewhere in the middle

49
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.620
of the cumuloregalis cloud.

50
00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.920
Wait, you mean we have
to travel even higher?

51
00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.980
That's what the Log
Pose says, at least.

52
00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.600
Did I hear you call me a moron?

53
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.020
[ZORO]
I dunno, didja?

54
00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.730
An ocean!

55
00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.110
[laughing]

56
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.100
Here I go! Cloud-ocean
swimming champ, Usopp!

57
00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.060
[LUFFY whistling]

58
00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.390
[CHOPPER]
Yay! You can do it!

59
00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.230
– [LUFFY] Go, Usopp!
– Hey, you can't swim here!

60
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.520
We still don't know
anything about this place.

61
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.480
Watch me!

62
00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.440
He did it!

63
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.520
He's so brave!

64
00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.280
[USOPP]
It's hard to see anything,

65
00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.160
but I'm really moving!

66
00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.120
There's so little resistance!

67
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.790
Wow, I'm just going deeper
and deeper. It's so easy!

68
00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.630
Aw, man. It's no fair.

69
00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:00.580
Hey, uh... He's not
comin' back up.

70
00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.080
You know, it's possible

71
00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.880
this ocean may not
have an actual bottom.

72
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.250
Say what?

73
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.130
Idiot! Did that fool just
fall through the clouds?

74
00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.700
Usopp!

75
00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.620
I just told him
not to go in there!

76
00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.720
Luffy! Stretch out
as far as you can!

77
00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.550
I am! But I can't
see where he is!

78
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.790
Just leave that part to me!

79
00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.800
Ojos Fleur!

80
00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.140
[ROBIN]
There he is!

81
00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.070
[LUFFY]
What? Where?

82
00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.260
[ROBIN]
Vente Fleur!

83
00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:50.970
[grunts]

84
00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.560
Okay. Now pull him up.

85
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.100
All right, I got him!

86
00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.930
[grunting]

87
00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.440
[CHOPPER]
Is he heavy?

88
00:05:58.570 --> 00:05:59.660
[ROBIN]
He shouldn't be that heavy.

89
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:00.580
[CHOPPER]
C'mon, Luffy!

90
00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.120
Pull harder!

91
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.090
Yes! He's back! Huh?

92
00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.380
[LUFFY]
But he's not alone!

93
00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.380
[NAMI screams]

94
00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.960
[SANJI]
They're trying to eat him!

95
00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.070
[BOTH screaming]

96
00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.550
[ZORO]
You hungry? Eat this!

97
00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:22.650
Huh?

98
00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:47.120
This air, it's so thin.

99
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.290
It's hard to breathe.

100
00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:49.660
[SANJI]
What do you make of this?

101
00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.620
It's the strangest
creature I've ever seen.

102
00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.720
I'm not even sure it's a fish.

103
00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.390
[LUFFY]
That octopus thing
was more like a big balloon.

104
00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.440
[ZORO]
Yeah, except balloons
don't have teeth.

105
00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.960
[NAMI]
But how can there be
fish up here in the clouds?

106
00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.360
[ROBIN]
You said it best yourself.

107
00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.260
Basically, it's an
ocean in the sky.

108
00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.470
[CHOPPER]
So what's this big snake thing?

109
00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.880
[LUFFY]
I dunno. A flatfish?

110
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:10.510
[CHOPPER]
But it wasn't
flat till Sanji kicked it.

111
00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.770
[screaming]

112
00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.290
Oh, come on, Usopp.
What is it this time?

113
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.800
[USOPP]
There's something in my pants!

114
00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.700
Usopp!

115
00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:25.540
Sky island scary.
Sky island scary...

116
00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.210
Not his day.

117
00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:30.120
Sky island scary.
Sky island scary...

118
00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.200
Hold on. Do you know
what this is?

119
00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.540
I think it's one
of the "skyfish"

120
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.170
Noland described in his log.

121
00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.180
It sounded pretty
fantastic at the time,

122
00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.750
but now that I see it,

123
00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.010
it looks like these creatures
have somehow actually evolved

124
00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.640
to survive up here
in the clouds.

125
00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.060
They evolved?

126
00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.770
You mean they turned all flat
and balloony and stuff?

127
00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.810
To make themselves even lighter.

128
00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:50.110
The buoyancy up here must
be several times weaker

129
00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.720
than in the oceans down below.

130
00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.390
And they grew scales
like feathers.

131
00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.750
And those weird
carnivore-like mouths.

132
00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:57.980
I tried sautéing it.

133
00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.020
Delicious!

134
00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.290
Hey! We were still
examining that!

135
00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.110
What were you guys thinking?

136
00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.720
Hm, wait. This is good!

137
00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.090
I've never tasted
anything like it!

138
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.120
[SANJI]
Well, you know me,
I aim to please.

139
00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.720
[LUFFY]
Ooh! Let's eat
that big one, too!

140
00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.970
[CHOPPER]
So, where's this "sky island"?

141
00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.850
Huh? What's that?

142
00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.230
A ship.

143
00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.230
Hey, guys! There's a...!

144
00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.140
[gasps]

145
00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.860
[CHOPPER screams]

146
00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.820
[SANJI]
Say, what's wrong Chopper?

147
00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.990
[SANJI]
What's the deal?
You see somethin' out there?

148
00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.910
Yeah! A ship! It was
there, but then it split!

149
00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.410
[ZORO]
Say what?

150
00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.670
And there's a bull with wings!
And he's running around...

151
00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.740
[ZORO]
You're talkin' crazy!
Calm down!

152
00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.830
What got into him?

153
00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.090
Check it out. He's right.

154
00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:47.190
There's a guy runnin'
around out there.

155
00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.090
Hey, stop! What do you want?

156
00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.360
[WYPER]
To destroy you!

157
00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.780
Oh, is that all?

158
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:52.660
He's mine.

159
00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.720
Who is? What's goin' on?

160
00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:03.380
[NAMI]
Hey! Don't let this
guy walk all over you!

161
00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.630
Get him!

162
00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:10.420
[CHOPPER screams]

163
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.070
He's gonna blow us up!

164
00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.320
Sky island scary.
Sky island scary.

165
00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.180
[GAN FALL]
That's enough, villain!

166
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.360
Oh, great! Now who's this guy?

167
00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.790
[GAN FALL]
Miss, you may
call me the Sky Knight.

168
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.220
He's gone.

169
00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.500
What's going on here?

170
00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.710
Who the heck was that guy?

171
00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.130
And you. Could you be
any more worthless?

172
00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.880
That was pathetic! You had him
outnumbered three to one!

173
00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.220
[CHOPPER]
You saved us! Thanks a lot!

174
00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.810
[GAN FALL]
I'm just doing my duty.

175
00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:07.060
This one's on the house.

176
00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.820
What gives? I feel so weak.

177
00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.020
[LUFFY]
Yeah.

178
00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:14.340
I... could barely move.

179
00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.420
[ROBIN]
It must be
because of the thin air.

180
00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:17.530
[ZORO]
What?

181
00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.670
Oh, yeah. I almost
forgot about that.

182
00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.490
[GAN FALL]
You must be Blue Sea People.

183
00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.740
[NAMI]
"Blue Sea People"? What's that?

184
00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:24.910
And who are you?

185
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.710
[GAN FALL]
As I said, I am the Sky Knight.

186
00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.920
And "Blue Sea People"
is what we call those

187
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.460
who live beneath the clouds.

188
00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.150
[GAN FALL]
I'm assuming
that you've traveled here

189
00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.730
from the blue sea.

190
00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.900
[LUFFY]
Yeah, that's right.

191
00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.360
[GAN FALL]
Then that explains it.

192
00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.400
You have reached the White Sea,
7,000 meters in the air.

193
00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.500
The White-White Sea, where
I assume you're heading,

194
00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.030
is still further up,
about 10,000 meters.

195
00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.410
Ordinary Blue Sea People can't
possibly endure it here.

196
00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.550
Okay, I think I've
gotten used to it.

197
00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.880
Yeah. I actually feel
much better already.

198
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.340
[GAN FALL]
No, no, no.
That's just not possible.

199
00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:55.910
[CHOPPER]
So, Mr. Knight,

200
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.540
why was that guy running around
in the clouds attacking people?

201
00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.510
[GAN FALL]
Now, now. Not so fast.

202
00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.140
No doubt you have
many questions,

203
00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.480
but first we have matters
of business to discuss.

204
00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:05.640
[NAMI]
Business?

205
00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.940
You see, I am a
soldier-for-hire.

206
00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:10.030
The White Seas can
be quite dangerous.

207
00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.600
There are guerillas
lurking about,

208
00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.150
like the one you've just faced,
who would like nothing more

209
00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.730
than to turn you into
food for the skyfish.

210
00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.480
But if you purchase a
5,000,000 Extol One Whistle,

211
00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.790
I'll protect you.

212
00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.000
[LUFFY]
Huh? What're you talkin' about?

213
00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:27.220
[GAN FALL]
Uh! Now, listen!
That price is quite reasonable!

214
00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.800
I can't afford to lower it
a single extol more!

215
00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.470
I have to earn a living, too.

216
00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.430
[SANJI]
Yeah, but what
the heck is an "extol"?

217
00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.080
And what's this "whistle"
thing or whatever?

218
00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.130
[GAN FALL]
You don't know?

219
00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.670
I don't understand...
you came here

220
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:40.960
from the summit of
High-West, didn't you?

221
00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.210
Surely you must have
passed an island or two.

222
00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.920
I still don't know what
you're talkin' about.

223
00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.510
Wait, let me get this straight.

224
00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:48.700
You're saying there's another
way we could've gotten up here

225
00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:51.030
where we would have passed
"an island or two"?

226
00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.450
As in there's more
than one sky island?

227
00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.890
[GAN FALL]
What? Don't tell
me you traveled by way of...

228
00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.640
[ROBIN]
We rode up on
the Knock-Up Stream.

229
00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.850
[GAN FALL]
My word. That monstrous current?

230
00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.440
So there are still souls
in the world brave enough

231
00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.440
to make the attempt.

232
00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.990
[NAMI]
I knew it! So we risked
are lives for nothing!

233
00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:10.110
Are you happy?!
We could've all been killed!

234
00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.660
If we'd just asked
around a little more,

235
00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.600
we could've found a
safer way to get here!

236
00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.890
Of all the reckless, stupid,
insane things to do!

237
00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.810
What were you thinking?

238
00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.710
[GAN FALL]
Did you lose any of your crew?

239
00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:21.550
No. We all made it.

240
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.890
Then you can consider
yourselves fortunate.

241
00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.210
Had you taken a different route,

242
00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.170
one or two of you would've
survived the journey,

243
00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.650
but the rest would've perished.

244
00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.240
That's the gamble.

245
00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.570
By way of the Knock-Up Stream,

246
00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:33.810
either everyone dies
or everyone survives.

247
00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.080
Those are the only two
possible outcomes.

248
00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.680
Not many are willing to accept

249
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.520
that sort of
all-or-nothing risk.

250
00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.130
Especially these days.

251
00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.980
If nothing else, I see now
that you are navigators

252
00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.690
of exceptional
bravery and skill.

253
00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.020
Yeah, well, I hate
to take all the credit,

254
00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.300
but see, when things got
scary and these guys

255
00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:52.980
were all screamin' and
cryin' for their mommies,

256
00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.980
I was the one who
stood up and said...

257
00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:56.360
Nothing at all!

258
00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.390
Thought so.

259
00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:59.100
[GAN FALL]
This is the One Whistle!

260
00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:02.720
It is yours to use
as you see fit.

261
00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.770
Should you find
yourselves in danger,

262
00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:07.370
you have but to blow it and
I will come to your aid!

263
00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:10.040
As I said, normally, I would
charge you five million extol,

264
00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:13.460
but for today, please accept
this as my gift to you.

265
00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:16.680
But wait! We still
don't know your name!

266
00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:21.310
I am Gan Fall. And this
is my partner Pierre!

267
00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.050
Pi-e!

268
00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:26.850
[GAN FALL]
Despite appearances,
Pierre is no ordinary bird.

269
00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.980
[GAN FALL]
Long ago,
he ate of a Horse-Horse Fruit

270
00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.060
and gained its powers.

271
00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.770
What? What powers?

272
00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.310
[GAN FALL]
He is able to transform

273
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.230
into a horse with wings!

274
00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:41.610
Namely...

275
00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.770
Oh! Wow! A Pegasus!

276
00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.440
[GAN FALL]
Yes! A Pegasus!

277
00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:49.020
[PIERRE]
Pi-e!

278
00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:51.900
[ALL]
– Wow, that's... something.
– Wow, that's... something.

279
00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:57.030
[GAN FALL]
May luck be
with you, brave warriors!

280
00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.660
[SANJI]
Am I the only one
who finds that bizarre?

281
00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.940
[ROBIN]
In the end, he really
didn't tell us anything, did he?

282
00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.900
[USOPP]
No. Nothing, actually.

283
00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.070
[SANJI]
Well, back to
square one, I guess.

284
00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.110
Yeah. Where are we supposed
to go from here?

285
00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.280
[LUFFY]
I know!

286
00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.930
Let's call the old man
back and ask him!

287
00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:14.400
Don't even think
about it, Luffy!

288
00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.260
You don't blow that whistle
to ask for directions!

289
00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.180
It's supposed to be for
emergencies only!

290
00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.760
Yeah!

291
00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.330
What if that guerilla guy who
attacked us comes back again?

292
00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.470
You wanna get blown up?

293
00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:26.100
I'll tell you what. For now,
let's just keep moving.

294
00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.380
[CHOPPER]
Hey, look over there, you guys!

295
00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:29.860
What is that?

296
00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.400
Some kinda' cloud.

297
00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.560
It looks more like a waterfall.

298
00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:37.740
[ZORO]
Okay, that settles
it. We go that way.

299
00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.040
Hey! Hold up!
Stop the boat here!

300
00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.050
[ROBIN]
Hmm. Looks like
the way's blocked.

301
00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:58.720
[CHOPPER]
What do we do?

302
00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.380
Those big clouds look
like they're floating

303
00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:02.550
on top of the ocean,
sorta like icebergs.

304
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:03.970
So, what? They're "cloud-bergs"?

305
00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.220
Well, there's obviously
something different about them.

306
00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.590
Maybe I can grab a piece.

307
00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:12.640
Gum-Gum... Pistol!

308
00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.010
It bounced off!

309
00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.770
[laughs]

310
00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.270
Ah!

311
00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.600
[LUFFY]
Hey, look! I'm not sinking!

312
00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:25.190
It's all fluffy and bouncy!
It's great! Ha!

313
00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.400
You guys outta try this!
Come on! It's fun!

314
00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.780
[LUFFY laughing]

315
00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.180
How does this work?

316
00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:31.990
It's a mystery.

317
00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.080
[USOPP]
Wa-hoo! Here I come!

318
00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.660
Me, too! Me, too!

319
00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.210
[sighs]

320
00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:42.210
So soft. It's like a gigantic
marshmallow pillow.

321
00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.660
Maybe I'll just
take a little nap.

322
00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:51.080
[ALL laughing]

323
00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:54.280
Hm. Well, we obviously can't
sail through these clouds,

324
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:57.040
so we'll have to find a way to
get around them somehow.

325
00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.930
Hey, you guys see
if you can spot a route

326
00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:01.140
the ship can take!

327
00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:02.220
Yeah! Right!

328
00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.140
[USOPP]
Luffy! Come check this out!

329
00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.310
What?

330
00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.560
[NAMI]
Where do you
think you're going?!

331
00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.600
Get back here!
Quit playing around!

332
00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.140
What in the world is that?

333
00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.360
[NAMI]
A gate?

334
00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.690
Yeah! A big one.

335
00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:17.730
It's up ahead, underneath
that waterfall thingy.

336
00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.190
[CHOPPER laughing]

337
00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:21.700
[SANJI]
So there's a man-made structure

338
00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.240
in the middle of the clouds?

339
00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:25.160
[ROBIN]
At this point, I'm not
sure anything we'd find up here

340
00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.030
would surprise me.

341
00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.830
[LUFFY]
Well, we'll see it soon enough!

342
00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.110
[CHOPPER]
Take a left next.

343
00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.080
[USOPP]
No, go right!

344
00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.160
[CHOPPER]
But it's to our left!

345
00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.790
[USOPP]
It's on the right!

346
00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.720
[LUFFY]
I'll call the old knight guy!

347
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.760
Hey. We're here.

348
00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:45.640
[ALL gasp]

349
00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.060
[SANJI]
Yep. That's a gate, all right.

350
00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.710
[NAMI]
And look.

351
00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:53.380
That weird cloud we saw really
is some kind of waterfall.

352
00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.680
It's coming down on top
of those "cloud-bergs."

353
00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.430
[USOPP]
Hold on, am I
reading this right?

354
00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:00.180
"Heaven's Gate"?
What's that all about?

355
00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.800
Sounds like a place
you go when you die.

356
00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.390
Yeah? Well now that
you mention it,

357
00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:06.640
maybe we are dead.
You ever think about that, huh?

358
00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:08.990
Oh. You know, that would
actually go a long way

359
00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.610
toward explaining
this weird place.

360
00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:11.910
But I don't wanna be dead!

361
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.370
[LUFFY laughs]

362
00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:15.480
Who cares? We're here, right?

363
00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:17.570
Wherever this gate
goes, I'm goin'.

364
00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.400
[NAMI]
Will you get serious?!

365
00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:20.650
[ZORO]
Ow! What was that for?

366
00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:22.740
[NAMI]
If you're making
a joke, it's not funny!

367
00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.370
[CHOPPER]
So, why'd you hit me, too?

368
00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:28.500
Wait! Over there!
There's somebody's coming out!

369
00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:36.150
<b>Inspector Amazon
Heaven's Gate</b>

370
00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:39.520
Wow. That's what sky people
look like? She's so wrinkly.

371
00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:41.810
State your business.

372
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.900
Sightseeing?
Warmongering? Other?

373
00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.880
It makes little difference.

374
00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.550
But if you wish to proceed,

375
00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.260
you must first pay
the entrance fee

376
00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:53.640
of one billion extol per person.

377
00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:54.770
That is the law.

378
00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.560
What?! One billion?!

379
00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.060
They're really big on these
extol things around here.

380
00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:00.690
I can't even count that high.

381
00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:02.690
I wonder how much that
would be in berries.

382
00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.500
It's got to be a lot.
I mean, a billion anything.

383
00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.400
It sounds expensive.

384
00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.190
A billion per person,
which makes seven blllion total.

385
00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.860
Something's fishy here.

386
00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.200
Seven billion just to go
through a stupid gate?

387
00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.740
I think this old bag's
trying to scam us...

388
00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.240
Listen, about the money.

389
00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.390
What if, you know,
we don't have it?

390
00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:24.610
You may still pass.

391
00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.900
What, seriously?

392
00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:26.980
[AMAZON]
The choice is yours.

393
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.570
I certainly won't
try to stop you.

394
00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.070
[NAMI, USOPP]
– Uh?
– Uh?

395
00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.120
My job description
does not require me

396
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.620
to actually guard the gate.

397
00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:36.820
I'm merely here to
ask your intentions.

398
00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:37.860
[LUFFY]
So that settles it!

399
00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.410
We wanna go to the sky islands!

400
00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:41.620
[USOPP]
But we don't have the
money, so we can't pay you!

401
00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.120
[AMAZON]
Very well.
The seven of you, then?

402
00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:46.960
Yeah.

403
00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.500
Except, we still need you to
tell us how to get there.

404
00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.540
[NAMI, CHOPPER, USOPP screaming]

405
00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.530
[LUFFY]
What the heck is that?

406
00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.830
The White Sea's
famous Express Lobster.

407
00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.700
[LUFFY, USOPP scream]

408
00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.830
[USOPP]
We're moving!

409
00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.440
[CHOPPER]
It's a giant lobster!

410
00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:08.120
[ZORO]
It's taking us up the waterfall!

411
00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:09.680
[NAMI]
Everybody hang on tight!

412
00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.220
[SANJI]
It's so fast!

413
00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:17.320
[USOPP screaming]

414
00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.720
[screaming]

415
00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.590
[AMAZON]
This is Heaven's
Gate inspector Amazon!

416
00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.140
Hear me now!

417
00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.160
To the almighty God above,
and his holy priests,

418
00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.120
I bear tidings!

419
00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:37.460
Seven illegal entrants have
passed into God's Land, Skypiea!

420
00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:41.510
Bestow upon them
Heaven's Judgment!

421
00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:50.310
[AMAZON]
Bestow upon
them Heaven's Judgment.
